  "created": "2019-08-02T04:24:01.473Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "(gesture equipment slots)\nHey there, I was wondering if there was a way to store gestures into the touch pad in a dynamic fashion.\n\nLike a drag-and-drop interface that some games have where you can move equipment into inventory slots.\n\nWhat I'd suggest is having 8 slots available on each Index controller, then give pictures for the gestures that are attached, and allow players to drag their pictures from the complete menu at the side, into the spaces on the touchpad in the center.\n\nThe transferred emotes should not be active on the main gesture list and only used by the touchpad. (Also only gestures for the correct hand should be put into the pad boxes)\n\nAnd because the pad is also a button, hovering over the section of the pad allows for preview mode (fast gestures), then clicking allows the gesture to stay put until the pad is touched (as it is not directly in the way of the hands most times.) Touch interrupt could have a toggle, so that only clicking the pad releases the prior emote.\n\nThis would free up the hand controllers, as well as allow us to custom fit the gestures of an avatar we may find in the \"Wild\".",
